<section class="plate" aria-labelledby="plate-2">
	<div class="wrap plate-mark">
		<p class="runhead"><span>Starbuck</span><span class="mid">What it checks</span><span>Plate II.</span></p>
		<h2 id="plate-2">Four questions for each reference.</h2>
		<ol class="levels">
			<li><span class="lv">Level 1</span><h3>Does it exist?</h3><p>The DOI, PMID, PMCID, arXiv ID or ISBN resolves. Without an identifier, Starbuck searches Crossref, PubMed, OpenAlex, DataCite and Open Library. A dead link gets its Wayback Machine copy.</p></li>
			<li><span class="lv">Level 2</span><h3>Does it match?</h3><p>The cited title, first author and year agree with the record. A real DOI that belongs to another paper is a Fail.</p></li>
			<li><span class="lv">Level 3</span><h3>Does it still stand?</h3><p>Retractions, expressions of concern and corrections, from Crossref with Retraction Watch data, PubMed and OpenAlex. A cited preprint with a published version gets a Note.</p></li>
			<li class="opt"><span class="lv">Level 4, optional</span><h3>Does it support the sentence?</h3><p>A language model reads the full text or the abstract and quotes the passage it relies on. Starbuck rejects a quote that is not in the source.</p></li>
		</ol>
		<p class="section-lead">It also lists citations without a reference, references that the text does not cite, and sentences that state a finding without a citation. <a href="/how-it-checks/">The rules</a>.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="plate" aria-labelledby="plate-3">
	<div class="wrap plate-mark">
		<p class="runhead"><span>Starbuck</span><span class="mid">What it reads</span><span>Plate III.</span></p>
		<div class="split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="plate-3">Write in the tool you use.</h2>
				<p class="section-lead">No export step. Starbuck reads the manuscript as you write it.</p>
				<ul class="result-points">
					<li><strong>Word.</strong> Citations inserted with Zotero, Mendeley or EndNote carry their records, so no bibliography file is needed. Without them, Starbuck reads numbered, superscript and author-year citations.</li>
					<li><strong>LaTeX.</strong> <code>\cite</code> in its natbib and biblatex forms, with the <code>.bib</code> files, or a <code>thebibliography</code> list.</li>
					<li><strong>Markdown and Quarto.</strong> Pandoc citations with BibTeX, CSL JSON or CSL YAML, and the numbered lists that AI research agents write.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="prose-block">
				<p>The report is a Quarto document that renders to one HTML page or to Word, with a JSON file for other tools. It starts with the references that need attention, each with the reason, the cited and the recorded details side by side, the sentence that cites it, and what to do.</p>
				<p><code>starbuck fix</code> turns the corrections that the records support into a diff of your <code>.bib</code>, CSL or Markdown file: a missing DOI, a wrong year, the published version of a preprint. It changes the file only with <code>--in-place</code>, and keeps a copy.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="plate" aria-labelledby="plate-4">
	<div class="wrap plate-mark">
		<p class="runhead"><span>Starbuck</span><span class="mid">Starbuck and Sub-Sub</span><span>Plate IV.</span></p>
		<h2 id="plate-4">Two tools from the same crew.</h2>
		<div class="pair">
			<div>
				<h3>Starbuck on its own</h3>
				<p>A command for the terminal, an MCP server for any AI agent, a GitHub Action and a pre-commit hook. For authors before submission, for co-authors, for editors and reviewers, and for agents that must check the sources they write.</p>
				<p><a href="/guide/">Guide</a> · <a href="/automate/">Automate</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="pair-box">
				<h3>Starbuck in Sub-Sub</h3>
				<p><a href="{{ site.subsub }}">Sub-Sub</a> is a research assistant that works from your own Zotero library. With reference checks on, its Researcher has <code>/verify</code>: Starbuck checks the manuscript, the model you use in Sub-Sub judges claim support, and Sub-Sub asks before a report or a correction is written outside your folders.</p>
				<p><a href="/sub-sub/">How they work together</a> · <a href="{{ site.subsub }}/install/#reference-checks-starbuck">Turn it on in Sub-Sub</a></p>
			</div>
		</div>
